<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Dithakong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1823</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mfecane">Mfecane</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Dithakong was fought in June 1823 near the Batlhaping town of Dithakong, in the north of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>. Mounted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/griqua">Griqua</a> gunmen, allied with the Batlhaping and called in through the missionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-moffat">Robert Moffat</a>, defeated a large force of displaced Sotho-Tswana groups driven west by the upheavals of the period, inflicting heavy losses.</p></div>
